id: pm-gh1585
title: "GH-1585: make tracked policy-refusal audit side effects explicit and actionable"
description: "A refused workflow mutation intentionally records policy_refused in tracked workspace history before throwing, while the refusal envelope does not disclose that write. Evaluate a compatible SDK-first policy for audit location, opt-in tracking or explicit side-effect receipts and repeated-attempt handling; preserve refusal evidence and item immutability. Intake only; no implementation or fix is claimed."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:governance",history,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-25T11:59:39.059Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T14:49:02.054Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-25T14:49:01.264Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T14:49:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Choose and document compatible refusal-audit semantics; expose any durable writes in typed SDK and transport diagnostics; cover repeated refusals and dry runs; retain item and item-history immutability; regression-test SDK, CLI and MCP in isolated trackers."
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
repro_steps: "External report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1585 reproduces on pinned 2026.10.20 and 2026.10.24: refuse close through required-field policy and inspect tracked workspace history. Current source confirms appendWorkspaceAuditEvent occurs before workflow_policy_refused is thrown; no independent sandbox execution has yet been performed for this intake."
resolution: "Workflow-policy errors expose tracker-relative side_effects with the exact sealed record hash, preserve typed CLI/MCP diagnostics and human guidance, retain per-attempt audits, and return an empty side-effect list for write-free dry-run refusals."
expected_result: A caller can identify every intentional refusal audit append and recover safely while item state and item history remain unchanged.
actual_result: "SDK, real CLI and MCP refusal controls pass; repeated attempts return their appended record evidence; item-history bytes and dry-run workspace history remain unchanged. All 23 initial focused and 87 revised acceptance tests pass, with linked owner execution passing. Advisory and required observability gates pass. Final hosted checks remain merge requirements."
